Signed-off-by: Julio Ramos <ramos.isw@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: antigravity:gemini-3.8-flash
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: SPL: when booted from MMC, register only the boot slot

With CONFIG_SPL_MMC_TINY there is a single static struct mmc, so the
lookup in spl_mmc.c ends up initialising whichever slot was registered.
Registering both slots at once causes brownouts and corrupts the static
struct mmc. Bring up ONLY the slot that the BROM booted from (MMC0 for SD
or MMC2 for eMMC) when CONFIG_SPL_MMC_TINY is enabled.

---
 board/sunxi/board.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

--- a/board/sunxi/board.c
+++ b/board/sunxi/board.c
@@ -509,6 +509,26 @@
 
 int board_mmc_init(struct bd_info *bis)
 {
+#ifdef CONFIG_XPL_BUILD
+	/*
+	 * In SPL with CONFIG_SPL_MMC_TINY, only one static struct mmc exists.
+	 * Bring up ONLY the slot that the BROM booted from, avoiding dual
+	 * initialization, brownouts, and struct mmc corruption.
+	 */
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SPL_MMC_TINY)) {
+		if (CONFIG_MMC_SUNXI_SLOT_EXTRA != -1 &&
+		    sunxi_get_boot_device() == BOOT_DEVICE_MMC2) {
+			mmc_pinmux_setup(CONFIG_MMC_SUNXI_SLOT_EXTRA);
+			return sunxi_mmc_init(CONFIG_MMC_SUNXI_SLOT_EXTRA) ? 0 : -1;
+		}
+
+		if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_UART0_PORT_F) &&
+		    sunxi_get_boot_device() == BOOT_DEVICE_MMC1) {
+			mmc_pinmux_setup(0);
+			return sunxi_mmc_init(0) ? 0 : -1;
+		}
+	}
+#endif
 	/*
 	 * The BROM always accesses MMC port 0 (typically an SD card), and
 	 * most boards seem to have such a slot. The others haven't reported
